message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "GeoExplain: Explainable Machine Learning for Geospatial Prediction"
abstract: >-
  GeoExplain is an open-source Python toolkit for explaining machine-learning predictions on
  geospatial data. Beyond global and local SHAP explanations it computes spatial SHAP layers that
  show where each variable contributes to a prediction, and it provides spatial validation,
  model comparison, reproducible workflows and an optional QGIS Processing provider.
